    <string name="session_permission_rationale_title">Show session notification actions?</string>
    <string name="session_permission_rationale_message">Android 13 and later uses notification permission to show XMouse-NG Open controls and Disconnect actions in the notification drawer. If you deny it, the foreground session can still run, but its notice is shown in Android Task Manager rather than the drawer. You can always disconnect from Session controls in XMouse-NG.</string>
    <string name="session_permission_request">Request permission</string>
    <string name="session_permission_continue_without">Continue without drawer actions</string>
    <string name="session_permission_denied_title">Notification permission denied</string>
    <string name="session_permission_denied_message">The foreground session may not appear in the notification drawer, so its Open controls and Disconnect actions may be unavailable there. Android still discloses the running foreground service in Task Manager. XMouse-NG Session controls remain available in the app.</string>
    <string name="session_permission_settings_title">Notification visibility is off</string>
    <string name="session_permission_settings_message">Android will not show another permission prompt after this choice. Open XMouse-NG notification settings to restore notification-drawer actions, or continue without them. The session remains disclosed by Android, and you can disconnect from Session controls in XMouse-NG.</string>
    <string name="session_permission_older_settings_message">This Android version does not use the notification runtime permission. Notification or channel settings may hide drawer actions; use Session controls in XMouse-NG to disconnect.</string>
